"""kilo_editor -- Kilo, a very small text editor, as a library: a translation of antirez's
kilo.c (https://github.com/antirez/kilo) to Adascript. The editor, and the loop that runs it.
It has no terminal in it; the program, kilo.ady, is one, a subclass of Terminal below.

    kilo <filename>

    ^S save      ^Q quit (three more presses when there are unsaved changes)
    ^F find      the arrows, ENTER and ESC in the search line: next, previous, stay, go back
    arrows, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown   move       Backspace, Del   delete

What is shown: the text in colour by language (C and C++, from the file's name: keywords,
types, strings, numbers, and // and /* */ comments, which run over lines), the status bar,
a message that fades after five seconds, and the search match.

Kilo is one file of C, a global struct and 1300 lines. Here the pieces are what they are:

    Look_T, Code_T, Key_T   how a character looks; what a terminal sends; what a key means
    Row                     a line of the file: its characters, how they are drawn, how they
                            look; a tab is one character in `chars` and up to eight in `render`
    highlight               how each character of a rendered line looks (editorUpdateSyntax)
    Editor                  the text, the cursor and what a key does to them
    Frame_T                 what the editor shows, handed to a terminal to draw
    Terminal, edit          what a terminal is asked for, and the loop that asks it

Kilo keeps one number for the cursor's column, `cx`, and uses it as a place in the line and as
a place on the screen; with a tab in the line the two differ, and kilo's search and its
scrolling go wrong there. Here the two are types of their own: Col_T is a place in a row's
`chars`, RCol_T is one in its `render`, and `Row.render_col` and `Row.col_of` are the only
way from one to the other. A key is decoded once into a Press_T, and a file that cannot be
read or written is a `| !PathFailure_T` where kilo calls perror and exits.

The differences from kilo are listed in README.md. In short: Home and End move (kilo
inserts a stray character), tabs stop at multiples of 8, a line comment inside a block comment
does not end the block, and a character that is not printable is shown reversed
in every file, not only in one with a language.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

